  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 309 PM MST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nWednesday...Our region will be in between weather disturbances with \na trough aloft over central Colorado, producing some cloud cover \nover our counties, but no precipitation. Temperatures slightly \nwarmer than Tuesday with 700 mb temperatures near 0 Celsius.\n\nThursday...High amplitude and well pronounced ridging aloft will \nprevail across our counties, keeping the weather dry. The warming \ntrend will continue, and with 700 mb temperatures near 2 Celsius, \nyielding maximum temperatures mainly in the 50s.\n\nFriday...A progressive and positively tilted shortwave trough aloft \nmoves across eastern Montana and eastern Wyoming, though with little \nif any cloud cover and no precipitation for our forecast area.\n\nSaturday...Brisk northwest flow aloft prevails, and with decent low \nlevel pressure gradients, look for a windy and blustery day. Maximum \ntemperatures should be slightly cooler than Friday.\n\nSunday...Transitory ridging aloft moves across our counties, with \nsignificant height rises aloft. 700 mb temperatures near 6 Celsius \nwill yield high temperatures from the lower 50s to lower 60s.\n\nMonday...The slow warming trend continues as the flow aloft backs to \nwesterly and with little if any cloud cover and 700 mb temperatures \nnear 5 Celsius suggesting maximum temperatures from the upper 50s to \nmid 60s.",
